# Staged by fisher-vls on 2026-11-26 for fisher-4h7.
# Acceptance from Stockfish 19 (sf_19, edb0d9d), Homebrew arm64 bottle,
# probed 2026-11-26: https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/releases/tag/sf_19
# Owner decision on fisher-4h7: over UCI, the duplicate letter KK grants the same
# kingside castling right as K on this position. See README.md for the
# source lines, the Stockfish captures and the move list below.
# The bare command a GUI sends to set the position up, with no moves.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4K2R w KK - 0 1
> go depth 1
# fisher-2aj rule 7 and the depth-1 totals in expectations/README.md: the
# node total at depth 1 is the number of legal moves at the root. With the
# kingside right there are 15, e1g1 among them; without it there are 14.
# python-chess 1.11.2 and Stockfish 19 go perft 1 both count 15 for K, KK
# and H, and 14 for -. Rule 2: no move captures, so every move leaves
# White up a rook (cp 500). The move stays open: rule 6 picks by
# the order of legal moves, which no expectation fixes (D48).
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 500 nodes 15 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
# Stockfish accepts this position and applies e1g1 with the same
# result as K. Without the right, e1g1 is illegal, and the owner decision
# for a rejected position sends one diagnostic before readyok.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4K2R w KK - 0 1 moves e1g1
> isready
# UCI isready/readyok, with no diagnostic before it.
< readyok
# The castled king on g1 and rook on f1 move on, and f1a1 checkmates
# Black. python-chess 1.11.2 and Stockfish 19 both report checkmate.
# A lost right, or a king or rook left elsewhere, makes a move illegal.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4K2R w KK - 0 1 moves e1g1 e8d8 g1f2 d8c8 f2e3 c8b7 e3d4 b7a6 d4c5 a6a5 f1a1
> go depth 1
# The owner approved this line on 2026-11-23 in a comment on fisher-2aj.2.
< info depth 0 score mate 0
# Owner-approved example for checkmate. UCI move format spells the null move 0000.
< bestmove 0000
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
